      "content": "That's a good start. I need a second case study to show as a comparison for the students—something that looks similar but involves a different demographic so they can practice identifying subtle differences in presentation.\n\nCan you do another one for a patient with the exact same symptoms? Severe sharp abdominal pain, similar vitals (maybe slightly higher pulse), and nausea/vomiting. Let's name this patient Marcus Washington, a 34-year-old Black male. Can you describe his behavior and how he's expressing the pain during the assessment?",
